HST Office: the Sheets header/footer edit page shows its "Preset", "Format" and "Field" labels and the Bold,
Italic and Underline button tooltips in the UI language instead of always in English.

Upstream sc/uiconfig/scalc/ui/headerfootercontent.ui leaves these six strings without translatable="yes", so no
message is extracted and the Vietnamese UI shows the English source. They become translatable with their own
contexts and get their Vietnamese text (glossary terms: Định dạng, Trường, Đậm, Nghiêng, Gạch dưới; "Định sẵn"
as in the page's own tip "Chọn một phần đầu hoặc phần chân định sẵn"). The image-only buttons take their
accessible name from the tooltip, so screen readers get the Vietnamese name too.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/unit/test_vi_sheets_headerfooter_labels.py; tests/runtime/check-vi-sheets-headerfooter-labels.py.
